   "design": "A program dashboard reads the booking system and survey tool and shows participation, retention and satisfaction per program, instead of exporting and computing in spreadsheets. Open feedback, with names and health details removed, is grouped into themes with example answers, and the coordinator reads a sample of each. The report starts from a draft whose figures trace to the measures. Benchmarks, discussions, conclusions, presenting and correspondence stay with the coordinator.",
   "approvals": [],
   "previous_blocker": "Figures were exported and computed by hand and feedback read one comment at a time.",
   "enabler_now": "Program dashboards and theme grouping of comments.",
   "still_hard": "Effects on health that participation figures do not show.",
   "human_edge": "Judging whether a popular program actually helps.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "decide_more_often",
    "what": "Evaluate each program every quarter instead of once a year."
   },
   "altitude": "Less computing and reading every comment; judgement stays.",
   "reach": [
    {
     "role": "management",
     "task": "Fund programs",
     "learn": "Whether evaluations come more often."
    }
   ],
